{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":60.11000061035156,"text":"In 1666, the Great Fire swept through London and the old cathedral burned down. The king asked Christopher Wren, who was an astronomer and mathematician as well as an architect, to design a new one. Wren worked for 35 years, and the cathedral was finished in 1710 with a dome 111 meters high, one of the biggest in the world. It is really three domes, one inside another, the one you see from outside, the one you see from inside, and a hidden brick cone between them that carries the weight. Climb 257 steps and you reach the Whispering Gallery, where a whisper against the wall travels all the way around to the far side. In the Second World War, bombs fell all around, but volunteers guarded the roof every night, and the dome survived. A photograph of it standing in the smoke gave courage to the whole country. Wren is buried in the crypt, and his tomb says, If you seek his monument, look around you.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.5400000214576721},{"word":"1666","start":0.5400000214576721,"end":1.8200000524520874},{"word":"the","start":2.180000066757202,"end":2.319999933242798},{"word":"Great","start":2.319999933242798,"end":2.680000066757202},{"word":"Fire","start":2.680000066757202,"end":3},{"word":"swept","start":3,"end":3.4000000953674316},{"word":"through","start":3.4000000953674316,"end":3.7799999713897705},{"word":"London","start":3.7799999713897705,"end":4},{"word":"and","start":4,"end":4.539999961853027},{"word":"the","start":4.539999961853027,"end":4.699999809265137},{"word":"old","start":4.699999809265137,"end":5.079999923706055},{"word":"cathedral","start":5.079999923706055,"end":5.340000152587891},{"word":"burned","start":5.340000152587891,"end":5.699999809265137},{"word":"down","start":5.699999809265137,"end":6.019999980926514},{"word":"The","start":6.71999979019165,"end":6.840000152587891},{"word":"king","start":6.840000152587891,"end":7.059999942779541},{"word":"asked"